`,v.jsx(e.p,{children:"In this tutorial, we will cover how to implement multitenancy in Qdrant. Multitenancy allows you to host multiple tenants or clients within a single instance of Qdrant, ensuring data isolation and access control between tenants. This feature is essential for use cases where you need to serve different clients while maintaining separation of their data."}),`
`,v.jsx(e.h2,{children:"Step 1: Create a collection"}),`
